ext": "<span class=\"strong\">Teacher</span>: Would you like to share the importance of layouts in HTML with us?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Leia</span>: Well, a layout is important to make a web page look better.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Teacher</span>: You have to explain that better.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Leia</span>: Sure, I would like to do it. I mean, it is what makes the website look attractive.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Teacher</span>: Right, even though modern websites are made with CSS and Java because they are more dynamic, you would also like to use simple HTML tables and its attributes combined with other tags to create useful layouts to your websites.</br>", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob07re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Leia</span>: Would you like to start telling us about the different layouts we can use in HTML, please?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Teacher</span>: Of course. There are three basic layouts in HTML: HTML layout using tables, multiple columns layout using table,s and HTML layouts using DIV, SPAN. The most conventional is the HTML < table > tag because it is arranged in rows and columns. I am going to explain the tags to you. Please, open a new file and we're going to try to do it together. Well, after the regular heading, within the < body > < /body > tags you place < table border=\"1\" > to start with the margin, and then between < tr > < /tr > tags you put < td >Row A, Column A< /td >, with that we have our first row and column so that we can write all the information we want.", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob07re2img02.jpg", "time": "37000", "id": 1}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Leia</span>: Teacher! I'm sorry, but something is not working here.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Teacher</span>: I'm coming\u2026 I see what the problem is. You have to make the table closing with the < /table > tag. Let's continue, you will do the same with the multiple column tag < title >Three Column HTML Layout< /title >, this will display menus, or even advertising if you want. The content appears in multiple pages. Finally, with the DIV, SPAN tag < title >HTML Layouts using DIV, SPAN< /title > which actually works better with CSS, you can group elements. Do you have any questions?</br>", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob07re2img03.jpg", "time": "132000", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe8n2le02ob07re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "_data": [], "id": 1, "template_override": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "HTML Layouts "}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you are talking about HTML layouts."}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Assess the incident of data in the macrosystem processes, based on the data dictionary to consolidate intervening data, based in established parameters."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.  Exchanges simple information on programming tools and solutions to a client's requirement."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Verbs with Infinitives, Would Like to, in Affirmative Statements and Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When there are two verbs together, the second one sometimes goes in the <span class=\"strong\">infinitive form</span> (<span class=\"italic\">to-</span>)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Would you like to share with us the importance of layouts in HTML?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sure, I would like to do it. I mean, it is what makes the website look attractive."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In order to use the <span class=\"strong\">infinitive form</span> of a verb within a sentence, there are few aspects we need to have in mind.</br></br> When you use the modal verb <span class=\"strong\">would</span> with a verb, the second verb always goes in the infinitive form. This is very typical with the combination <span class=\"strong\">would like to</span>. We use this form to either <span class=\"strong\">ask</span> or to <span class=\"strong\">say</span> something in a polite way.</br><br /> Examples:<br />"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Would</span> you <span class=\"strong\">like to use</span> HTML instead of JAVA? </br>Sarah <span class=\"strong\">would like to make</span> her website with HTML.</span></div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are also other verbs that are <span class=\"strong\">always</span> followed by the <span class=\"strong\">infinitive form</span>. There is no special rule for these, you have to memorize them. </br><br /> Example:<br />"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">want to know</span> how to use HTML and CSS properly.</span></div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The following are some common verbs which are always followed by the infinitive: "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Verbs Followed by Infinitive</span></div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"agree</br>  appear</br>  arrange</br>  ask </br> care</br>  choose</br>   claim</br>  decide</br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"demand</br>  deserve</br>  expect</br>   fail</br>  happen</br>  hesitate</br>  hope</br>  intend</br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" know</br> how</br>  learn</br>  manage</br> offer</br>  plan</br>  prepare</br>   pretend</br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"promise</br>  refuse</br>  seem</br>  swear</br>  try</br>  threaten</br>   undertake</br> want</br> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Commands for Different Types of HTML Layouts"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are three types of commands of HTML layouts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Layouts are very important to give a nice look to a website. In HTML we can find three types of layouts and you will see the commands in the chart below.<br /> "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">LAYOUT COMMAND</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">DESCRIPTION</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"< table > < /table >\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"HTML Layout - Using Tables\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"< table > < /table > < tr > < /tr > < td > < /td >\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Multiple Columns Layout - Using Tables\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"< div >< /div > < span > < /span >\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"HTML Layouts - Using DIV, SPAN\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The most conventional is the HTML tag because it is arranged in rows and columns."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Start with the margin and then between < tr > < /tr > tags you put < td > Row A."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A layout is important when we want to make a web page look better."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "website "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "group of web pages joined by links and placed on the World Wide Web"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Modern websites are made with CSS and Java because they are more dynamic. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "attractive "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having the quality to produce interest"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is what makes the website look attractive."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "combined "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "made by two or more features"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You would also like to use simple HTML tables and its attributes combined with other tags to create useful layouts to your websites."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "conventional "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used by most people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The most conventional is the HTML < table > tag."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rows"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a number of things in a line"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: the HTML < table > tag is arranged in rows and columns."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "margin "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a border outside the written matter"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You put < td >Row A, Column A< /td >, with that we have our first row and column so that we can write all the information we want."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Select two different websites you would have to create. Brainstorm your layout ideas."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make drawings two pages in which you show your possible layout."}, {"type": "text", "content": "What layout would you use? Why? How would you write it? Share your ideas with your classmates."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can define specific layouts according to the website needs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can demonstrate in a sketch what my final product will be."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can explain my design and describe the layout I would like to use."}]}]}